  "package_id": "berge-c4-saturation",
  "formal_scope": "Lean 4.35.0 proves, for actual three-uniform hypergraphs on Fin n, Berge-C₄s with distinct vertices and distinct hyperedges, and saturation under every absent triple, that for every n ≥ 9 a saturated hypergraph with ⌈(3n − 9)/4⌉ hyperedges exists, together with the general rooted-gluing theorem, the exact values for n ≤ 5 and the upper bounds for n = 6, 7, 8; explicit pieces are kernel-checked without native_decide. The lower bound, the cone classification and spectrum and the flexible-root theorem have conventional proofs, and the values for 6 ≤ n ≤ 13 rest on exhaustive certificates checked by an independent C++ verifier.",
